            {
                "entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                "word": "непрерывно",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3e25ae6-4531-3cba-bab4-0cbc54b9e639",
                        "entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "идя сплошным потоком; без промежутков"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef7ca31a-8b01-3732-9859-9ab8b3dbc46b",
                        "entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. не имея перерывов; не прекращаясь, беспрестанно"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db42d212-1452-4ee0-844a-aeb7e416227d",
                                "sense_id": "ef7ca31a-8b01-3732-9859-9ab8b3dbc46b",
                                "text": "Он непрерывно занимался трёпом, иной раз небезобидным: всячески разыгрывал напыщенного комсомольского деятеля Петушкова («Наш приятель Петушков без задорин и сучков»), влюбил в себя маленькую, хрупкого вида девочку, и потом отверг её в тот самый момент, когда она готова была ему принадлежать."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a2071c6-74d7-4eb1-ac4e-cd34765f20ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "uninterruptedly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "uninterruptedly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bd6c37c-9d51-3746-aa92-ee856a5b268f",
                                        "entry_id": "dd100f6a-3b6d-3f87-9b39-2bbe467cbf65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without interruption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9354cff2-65b2-46b4-ad66-93900338badb",
                                                "sense_id": "2bd6c37c-9d51-3746-aa92-ee856a5b268f",
                                                "text": "They adopted the singular, though in their case probably advantageous, decision to continue each to have a separate place of abode, in order that each might work uninterruptedly, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f267a351-fafc-46c8-b117-c718e674f0a8",
                                                "sense_id": "2bd6c37c-9d51-3746-aa92-ee856a5b268f",
                                                "text": "Speed downhill was not allowed to exceed 77½ m.p.h., then, after a 63 m.p.h. slowing through Creil, the more gradual rise to Gannes was climbed at between 75 and 79 m.p.h. uninterruptedly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "667eb6ab-982d-48eb-b527-70181faaf1dd",
                                                "sense_id": "2bd6c37c-9d51-3746-aa92-ee856a5b268f",
                                                "text": "Save for the three brief ¼-mile descents, before Bakewell, Monsal Dale and Miller's Dale, the line is climbing uninterruptedly at round about 1 in 100 for 9 miles from Rowsley almost to Miller's Dale, [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "44a03e67-9f26-40e0-9ab2-d75cd657f393",
                        "source_entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "continuously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "continuously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b57111cb-32df-399d-b33c-2a81e071db8b",
                                        "entry_id": "67d61252-9945-34ea-a8f4-233d95259065",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without pause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a3f9061-309d-45bb-812d-f6df62058290",
                                                "sense_id": "b57111cb-32df-399d-b33c-2a81e071db8b",
                                                "text": "The river continuously flows to the sea, it will never pause to let us cross on dry land."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bf09a40-14e7-44b1-b69f-518f212f4abe",
                                                "sense_id": "b57111cb-32df-399d-b33c-2a81e071db8b",
                                                "text": "In the year 1633, the Bridget Nuns, near Xanthus, behaved like sheep, jumping about and bleating continuously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05a70050-46b3-4ba7-889e-f8bdfbe2c66c",
                                                "sense_id": "b57111cb-32df-399d-b33c-2a81e071db8b",
                                                "text": "\"We continuously strive to improve our processes and indeed have updated our systems accordingly. Ultimately, however, it is for the student to make a proper declaration to SLC [Student Loans Company]^([sic]) to draw down funding,\" LSST said in a statement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43a83ba4-0fdc-481e-b769-73cba164ad42",
                        "source_entry_id": "53400fab-9118-352b-abaa-5f33f83a8ad9",
                        "target_lang_word": "incessantly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incessantly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                        "entry_id": "1c0b5e0c-ce41-3dbd-9e12-4edd7241bf72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a manner without pause or stop, especially to the point of annoyance; not ceasing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8942fe8-0ec5-4c4c-994d-570e2a765d3f",
                                                "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                                "text": "He jabbered incessantly and annoyed everyone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "536a0ccc-3282-4737-88a6-732bbbeeeadf",
                                                "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                                "text": "We see the eye subdued, the practised smile, / The word well weighed before it pass the lip, / And know not of the misery within: / Yet there it works incessantly, and fears / The time to come; for time is terrible, / Avenging, and betraying."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e14b3c7-51e7-4df8-aa70-a7cd7fc6aace",
                                                "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                                "text": "There were the tawny rocks, like lions couchant, defying the ocean, whose waves incessantly dashed against and scoured them with vast quantities of gravel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9c7e3be-79a0-4415-a38f-d8f664b958e3",
                                                "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                                "text": "\"You are old, Father William,\" the young man said, / \"And your hair has become very white; / And yet you incessantly stand on your head— / Do you think, at your age, it is right?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9c5f751-e862-4067-8772-2e8d94d1463f",
                                                "sense_id": "609e7f3d-9a0a-3a8c-b720-4ebe9a4fa969",
                                                "text": "But just there a small hairy terrier exploded out at the gate, like a floor-mop impelled by some sort of internal combustion, which sent him off into a frenzy of yapping, incessantly jerked backwards by the explosive force of his own detonations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fabb34e-2301-3f1c-94da-4807df624300",
                                        "entry_id": "1c0b5e0c-ce41-3dbd-9e12-4edd7241bf72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immediately."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
